  "label": "Christians are mapped onto the roadside memorial scene",
  "description": "The text 'ever notice that christians are bad drivers' is overlaid on an image of a roadside memorial with a school bus in the background. The visual material (roadside memorial scene) is being mapped onto the textual concept (stereotype_christians_bad_drivers) by implying that the tragic event (memorial) is caused by or associated with Christians being bad drivers. This creates an analogical mapping where the memorial scene (a symbol of tragedy) is being used to represent or stand in for the stereotype about Christians' driving behavior.",
